As a special case of Theorem~\ref{thm:main}, we know that all torus knots are characterized by their 0-traces, but the proof makes essential use of the fact that $S^3_0(T_{p,q})$ is a fibered 3-manifold.  Similarly, Theorem~\ref{thm:negtracetorus} tells us that positive torus knots are characterized by any of their negative traces, but reveals very little about their positive traces.  However, in some cases we can say a bit more about these positive traces.  In this section we will prove Theorem~\ref{thm:positive-trace-t2n-main}, which we restate here:

